{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments","id":1077525,"title":"Guidelines for Especially Useful Legacy Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T22:05:31-07:00","id":1077525,"title":"Guidelines for Especially Useful Legacy Attainments","content":"Considering the special mechanics of legacy attainments, I'd like to discuss the rules of thumb for designing ones that are mechanically appealing.<br /> <br /> I'm still learning so I'd appreciate corrections and alternative ideas.<br /> <br /> I make the assumption that a legacy attainment should be useful to a mage who meets the minimum requirements to learn it, so low-rank attainments should be useful with few dots in the primary arcanum of the legacy.<br /> <br /> The main constraints are the spell factor limitations:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Per the errata, legacy attainments gain primary ranks equal to dots in the relevant arcanum <b>minus one</b></li> <li>Legacy attainments spell factor ranks cannot be increased through yantras, teamwork, or extended ritual casting</li> <li>I assume that activating a legacy attainment is not a spellcasting roll and therefore it's not possible to achieve an Exceptional Success using the automatic successes you get from arcanum dots</li> <li>If the effect is Duration primary, it will have negligible Potency (at best Potency 3 for a Master)</li> <li>If the effect is Potency primary, it's possible to spend reach on Advanced Duration to still get a a reasonable duration. Otherwise, only a Master can eek out a three-turn duration.</li> </ol>These are the main benefits:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No chance of failure, unless Withstood (if relevant)</li> <li>No paradox</li> <li>No wisdom loss</li> <li>No possibility of counter-spelling or dispelling</li> <li>Does not count against gnosis-defined spell control limit</li> </ol>Finally, there is the rule that the Reach allowed for each attainment gets calculated by subtracting from the rank of the attainment the rank of the Practice it utilizes. That's okay because a number of reach options are pointless for legacy attainments: Advanced Potency, Indefinite Duration, exceeding spell control slots, and probably Advanced Scale.<br /> <br /> So I think you get these heuristics:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Withstood effects are less desirable.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Because Spirit effects that cross the Gauntlet get Withstood by Gauntlet strength, special care must be taken when defining Spirit-based legacies. The attainments should focus on affecting subjects in Twilight or the Fallen World. Because of the purview of Spirit (Essence, spirits, the Shadow, the Gauntlet), most Spirit effects are Withstood either by the subject or the Gauntlet itself.</li> <li>For other arcanum, attainments of Rank 1 - 3 should probably be designed <b>not</b> to be Withstood. Many Compelling, Ruling, and Fraying effects will not make good Legacy attainments unless reserved for rank 4 or 5, where you can assume that the mage acquiring that rank will have 4 or 5 dots in the relevant arcanum.</li> </ol></li> <li>Duration-primary effects that provoke Clash of Wills are highly desirable.</li> <li>Buffs are highly desirable because they cannot be dispelled and do not count against the normal spell control limit</li> </ol>So typically when building mechanically-appealing legacy attainments, I think these are useful suggestions:<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 1</b><br /> <br /> Reasonable options:<ul><li>A Knowing effect</li> <li>A Compelling effect that acts on the passive environment (these are typically Duration-primary)</li> <li>A Compelling effect that acts upon the caster herself</li> </ul>For a Spirit-primary legacy, the first attainment is pretty much always going to be a variation of Exorcist's Eye; there just isn't another effective option given the purview of Spirit. For a Forces-primary legacy you can Compel because the subject forces do not Withstand casting.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the mage who merely meets the prerequisites of the attainment, the Knowing spell will typically give the best bang for the buck. For example, Craftsman's Eye is fine with one Potency and a one-turn duration. Cleanse the Body will only work out if such a mage can perfectly time the use of the attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 2</b><br /> <br /> The best option is probably a Ruling spell that does not involve Withstand. Shielding and Veiling effects are better saved for the next rank when you can spend reach to get Advanced Duration for the CoW bonus, but you could also do them at Rank 2 and accept that you'll need to spend a scene activating the attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> <br /> This is a great rank for a Duration-primary Shielding or Veiling spell that provokes CoW, e.g. Mental Shield. Spend the free reach on Advanced Duration and instant casting time. Even a mage who merely meets the requirements for the attainment will get a +1 bonus to CoW and shield or veil can't be dispelled. The CoW bonus increases (a little) as the mage increases dots in the primary arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 4</b><br /> <br /> This is a great rank for a Perfecting self-buff. If the buff is Duration primary, consider spending the two reach to swap the primary factor to Potency and to give it Advanced Duration. If the buff is already Potency primary, then go for Advanced Duration and Instant Casting, OR consider making it the Rank 3 attainment instead. Either way, it results in a long-lasting buff that cannot be dispelled and does not consume a spell control slot.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 5</b><br /> <br /> I would use this one for a purely thematic effect since most mage characters will not get Gnosis 8 anyway, and if they do then they don't need to lean on their last legacy attainment for actual utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":"added note about Exceptional Success 04-13-2017, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:29:11-07:00","id":1077534,"title":"","content":"I thought Legacy Attainments didn't roll dice? When number of successes matter, the mage gains automatic successes equal to her dots in the Attainment's required Arcanum. (So a Master is always getting exceptional successes)<br /> <br /> For Withstand ratings, in my homebrews I often slip in an option to bypass them by meeting certain conditions. Conditions which compel the mage to act in certain behavioral patterns that fit the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I agree with most of these. But then again, I sometimes throw out performance optimality just for cool factors. Not that optimality is wrong, of course. Even in-universe, Attainments are a great lure for gathering new initiates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T23:59:22-07:00","id":1077546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077534#post1077534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Legacy Attainments didn't roll dice? When number of successes matter, the mage gains automatic successes equal to her dots in the Attainment's required Arcanum. (So a Master is always getting exceptional successes)<br /> <br /> For Withstand ratings, in my homebrews I often slip in an option to bypass them by meeting certain conditions. Conditions which compel the mage to act in certain behavioral patterns that fit the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I agree with most of these. But then again, I sometimes throw out performance optimality just for cool factors. Not that optimality is wrong, of course. Even in-universe, Attainments are a great lure for gathering new initiates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, does that mean it IS possible to negate withstand using an attainment if it is done by a master? Or is that only an option with normal spells because, well, you won't be choosing &quot;increase reach&quot; or &quot;increase spellfactors&quot; like you do with normal spells?<br /> <br /> ____<br /> <br /> So about legacies. What's with the three-turn/three-potency thing? I get the minus one part but wouldn't that be, um, 4? I noticed it in the corebook too but it confused me cuz I thought it was an error that escaped the errata.<br /> It sounds REALLY difficult to make certain attainments useful, or even certain legacy concepts all but impossible, even for gnosis 8 mages.<br /> Why is indefinite duration useless for attainments? I thought that would be coveted, even if it requires adding mana to the attainment.<br /> <br /> rank 2 stuff : You mention the clash of wills bonus for extended duration. Do you mean +1 for day, +2 for week, +4 for year, that sorta thing (I might have gotten the numbers wrong but, I hope you get my point). Wouldnt' those be useless if the clash of wills successes are automatically set to the dots of your arcanum? or do the &quot;automatic successes&quot; never apply to a Clash of Wills?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:39:28-07:00","id":1077556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077546#post1077546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woah, does that mean it IS possible to negate withstand using an attainment if it is done by a master? Or is that only an option with normal spells because, well, you won't be choosing &quot;increase reach&quot; or &quot;increase spellfactors&quot; like you do with normal spells?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to that rule where an exceptional success on a spell allows the caster to bypass Withstand? If so, then I see why not. Masters are not to be trifled with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:57:00-07:00","id":1077561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077556#post1077556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you referring to that rule where an exceptional success on a spell allows the caster to bypass Withstand? If so, then I see why not. Masters are not to be trifled with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if an archmage who doesn't have a legacy yet decides to make one, they can basically just disrupt all of the above heuristics and make whatever broken attainment they want and just go on a miracle-journey across the cosmos with their paradox-free, pax-free magic...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:40:22-07:00","id":1077576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077556#post1077556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you referring to that rule where an exceptional success on a spell allows the caster to bypass Withstand? If so, then I see why not. Masters are not to be trifled with.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say that activating an attainment is the same as casting a spell then it actually starts becoming an ES at 3 dots instead of mastery because attainments are made of modified Praxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:53:07-07:00","id":1077599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077561#post1077561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if an archmage who doesn't have a legacy yet decides to make one, they can basically just disrupt all of the above heuristics and make whatever broken attainment they want and just go on a miracle-journey across the cosmos with their paradox-free, pax-free magic...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what they're pretty much doing?<br /> <br /> I suppose the Pax Arcanum stops them from too much miracle journeys. And it could be that Imperial Spells (Arcanum 6+) still need Quintessence or can't be made into Attainments, since we don't know how archmages in 2e function. Lastly, I always assume creatures of such cosmic power are both too rare to be of concern to most people, and are often minding their own business instead of directly meddling with others. But this is just my preference on how things like this work, so YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:55:32-07:00","id":1077600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077576#post1077576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you say that activating an attainment is the same as casting a spell then it actually starts becoming an ES at 3 dots instead of mastery because attainments are made of modified Praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew that they were modified spells, but modified Praxes?<br /> <br /> Hmm.. has anyone covered this before? All I'm sure is that Attainments don't need to roll dice pools, and if they need successes they use the mage's Arcanum dots. Perhaps I'm missing something. Maybe exceptional successes don't count as &quot;needing&quot; successes? (This is hair-splitting, rules-lawyer stuff, but hey it does make some sense...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:59:54-07:00","id":1077601,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong, but I don't think activating an attainment is a spellcasting roll. Based on the language in the book, I don't think that you're meant to achieve Exceptional Success from activating a legacy attainment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>If</b></u> the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Sounds to me more like &quot;If for some weird reason it comes up...&quot; rather than &quot;For using with this important and obvious feature of the game that will come up all the time for Masters...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dice pools&quot; language by me was sloppy. I just meant the low cap on spell factors. I'm going to edit that to avoid confusion. It is primarily a limitation because I assume that legacy attainments do not have a way to avoid Withstand under RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T03:08:06-07:00","id":1077605,"title":"","content":"Okay so, if you have an Attainment and your primary spellfactor is potency, and you're a Master of this arcanum, why do you have potency 3 instead of potency 5, or even potency 4?<br /> with improvised magic, you have a minus 1 to the spellfactor anyway, right? Cuz the phrase is something like, you get the base factors, then a bonus equal to ranks on the spellfactors -1, right? So a Master's spells are often potency 5 if the spell uses potency as its primary factor right?<br /> <br /> So if the attainment rules mean minus 1 ontop of what you expect, that would be... potency 4. So why is it potency 3 is the limit? and why is it even lower for the secondary spellfactor, making it 2 turns?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:29:15-07:00","id":1077625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077605#post1077605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so, if you have an Attainment and your primary spellfactor is potency, and you're a Master of this arcanum, why do you have potency 3 instead of potency 5, or even potency 4?<br /> with improvised magic, you have a minus 1 to the spellfactor anyway, right? Cuz the phrase is something like, you get the base factors, then a bonus equal to ranks on the spellfactors -1, right? So a Master's spells are often potency 5 if the spell uses potency as its primary factor right?<br /> <br /> So if the attainment rules mean minus 1 ontop of what you expect, that would be... potency 4. So why is it potency 3 is the limit? and why is it even lower for the secondary spellfactor, making it 2 turns?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was talking about Potency as the secondary factor can only hit 3 if you round up.<br /> <br /> Primary Factor is Arcana-1 because if it followed normal rules you'd actually end up with a Primary Factor of Arcana +1 since a spell that scores a success is automatically counted as having achieved Duration 1, and Potency 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-13-2017, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:31:12-07:00","id":1077628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077600#post1077600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I knew that they were modified spells, but modified Praxes?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you develop an attainment it's specifically called out in the book as being developed from a Praxes and then the rules tell you how to modify it from a Praxes into an attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:23:48-07:00","id":1077643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077546#post1077546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> rank 2 stuff : You mention the clash of wills bonus for extended duration. Do you mean +1 for day, +2 for week, +4 for year, that sorta thing (I might have gotten the numbers wrong but, I hope you get my point). Wouldnt' those be useless if the clash of wills successes are automatically set to the dots of your arcanum? or do the &quot;automatic successes&quot; never apply to a Clash of Wills?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills is a contested roll-off of Gnosis + Arcanum. That series of contested rolls is unrelated to the original roll to cast the spell that provoked the CoW or the activation of an attainment. The bonus from Advanced Duration that I describe affects the CoW roll-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:31:29-07:00","id":1077648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077625#post1077625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He was talking about Potency as the secondary factor can only hit 3 if you round up.<br /> <br /> Primary Factor is Arcana-1 because if it followed normal rules you'd actually end up with a Primary Factor of Arcana +1 since a spell that scores a success is automatically counted as having achieved Duration 1, and Potency 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like an idiot. I think your explanation only made me feel more confused. Is this saying that legacies have less potency than a improvised spell that has no dice penalties? Like if you have a choice between casting something as an attainment or as an improvised spell and your, say, Forces is 4, what's the base potency of the spell in either case? Cuz I thought it was 4 in both cases, 4 potency as an attainment, or 4 potency as an improvised spell (unless you take penalties to increase spellfactors.)<br /> <br /> I still have no idea why the secondary factor is 2 less than the primary factor... Other than it just saying &quot;do it?&quot; When I first read legacies, I thought &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; meant something like, if your secondary spellfactor is duration and your 5th attainment uses a 3rd dot spell, then the secondary spellfactor will have 3 ranks to it (say 3 turns or a week duration), because the lowest requirement is 3 dots if it is a 3 dot spell being used for the attainment--meanwhile potency will be whatever your actual arcanum dots are, 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> So before reading this topic, I thought the legacy attainment would work like this---If you have primary factor potency, and used advanced duration reach, and are a Master of Forces, your spell will have 5 potency and could last 1 year. In the book, the example says it will last 3 turns, but I don't understand why, unless &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; means that the example attainment was a 3 dot spell and then that would make it last 3 turns?<br /> So in my example, does the 1 year duration or a 1 week duration depend wholly on whether this attainment is the 5th or the 3rd?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077643#post1077643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clash of Wills is a contested roll-off of Gnosis + Arcanum. That series of contested rolls is unrelated to the original roll to cast the spell that provoked the CoW or the activation of an attainment. The bonus from Advanced Duration that I describe affects the CoW roll-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I guess the Eleventh Question's 1st attainment that uses optional matter isn't a clash of wills? It did not say it was, so I guess not, but I assumed because using mage sight to pierce supernatural concealment normally calls for one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 04-13-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:34:37-07:00","id":1077650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077546#post1077546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is indefinite duration useless for attainments? I thought that would be coveted, even if it requires adding mana to the attainment.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's useless because under the rules it's not possible to get enough ranks in Duration to achieve the indefinite level unless Duration is the primary spell factor and the casting mage has <b>seven dots</b> in the relevant arcanum. The 2E rules don't provide a system for achieving such a rating. You can port the archmastery rules, but most players aren't involved in such a game anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:43:54-07:00","id":1077654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077648#post1077648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I guess the Eleventh Question's 1st attainment that uses optional matter isn't a clash of wills? It did not say it was, so I guess not, but I assumed because using mage sight to pierce supernatural concealment normally calls for one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Since legacy attainments can be arbitrarily &quot;atypical&quot; according to the rules, an attainment description can modify the rules in any way that your ST will permit. The only restriction is &quot;These adjustments shouldn\u2019t make Attainments significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems to me like a rough edge on the system in the core rulebook that the designer encountered even in defining their prototype 2E legacy, but decided not to resolve in the general rules for legacy attainments. It too wish that the designers had explicitly covered CoW in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:47:29-07:00","id":1077656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077648#post1077648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like an idiot. I think your explanation only made me feel more confused. Is this saying that legacies have less potency than a improvised spell that has no dice penalties? Like if you have a choice between casting something as an attainment or as an improvised spell and your, say, Forces is 4, what's the base potency of the spell in either case? Cuz I thought it was 4 in both cases, 4 potency as an attainment, or 4 potency as an improvised spell (unless you take penalties to increase spellfactors.)<br /> <br /> I still have no idea why the secondary factor is 2 less than the primary factor... Other than it just saying &quot;do it?&quot; When I first read legacies, I thought &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; meant something like, if your secondary spellfactor is duration and your 5th attainment uses a 3rd dot spell, then the secondary spellfactor will have 3 ranks to it (say 3 turns or a week duration), because the lowest requirement is 3 dots if it is a 3 dot spell being used for the attainment--meanwhile potency will be whatever your actual arcanum dots are, 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> So before reading this topic, I thought the legacy attainment would work like this---If you have primary factor potency, and used advanced duration reach, and are a Master of Forces, your spell will have 5 potency and could last 1 year. In the book, the example says it will last 3 turns, but I don't understand why, unless &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; means that the example attainment was a 3 dot spell and then that would make it last 3 turns?<br /> So in my example, does the 1 year duration or a 1 week duration depend wholly on whether this attainment is the 5th or the 3rd?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm. I guess the Eleventh Question's 1st attainment that uses optional matter isn't a clash of wills? It did not say it was, so I guess not, but I assumed because using mage sight to pierce supernatural concealment normally calls for one...</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, regular spells also rate at Primary Factor of Arcana -1 because a spell absolutely requires a minimum of factors at 1 which comes automatically with a successful casting.<br /> <br /> 2) Secondary factors in regular spells and attainments are always less than the Primary Factor because they receive the bump up in steps to Arcana -1 automatically, secondary factors are always bought up from 1 to X by accruing dice penalties. Attainments have an automatic formula for determining how many secondary factors can be &quot;bought&quot; up by saying that it's half the Arcana rating. So at Mastery half of 5 is 2.5, depending on the ST that can mean either 2 or 3 for automatic secondary factors.<br /> <br /> Looking at the PDF now though I think you're right, secondary factors calculation that I'm referring to is an artifact from my memory of the advance PDF and it was simplified for the final download. So secondary factors vary depending on the level of the prerequisite arcana for using it and are fixed instead of growing along with arcana rating like it used to. Downside, low rating attainments are screwed on secondary factors, upside high rating attainments get a significant boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:47:54-07:00","id":1077657,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind, covered better by Mrmdubois.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-13-2017, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:48:54-07:00","id":1077660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077650#post1077650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's useless because under the rules it's not possible to get enough ranks in Duration to achieve the indefinite level unless Duration is the primary spell factor and the casting mage has <b>seven dots</b> in the relevant arcanum. The 2E rules don't provide a system for achieving such a rating. You can port the archmastery rules, but most players aren't involved in such a game anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... so, similarly, this means that if someone with 7 dots was using potency instead of duration for the primary factor, then the potency is 6 right? It takes an archmaster with 7 dots in an arcanum to get an indefinite attainment (unless lasting was an option), or, 6 potency. So this means that a mage just starting in their legacy, with 2 dots in the legacy's arcanum will get their first attainment as something that only ever has 1 potency or 1 turn/hour durations right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:59:05-07:00","id":1077669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077660#post1077660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay... so, similarly, this means that if someone with 7 dots was using potency instead of duration for the primary factor, then the potency is 6 right? It takes an archmaster with 7 dots in an arcanum to get an indefinite attainment (unless lasting was an option), or, 6 potency. So this means that a mage just starting in their legacy, with 2 dots in the legacy's arcanum will get their first attainment as something that only ever has 1 potency or 1 turn/hour durations right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Potency bump would be 6, but the total Potency would be 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:07:39-07:00","id":1077674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077656#post1077656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) No, regular spells also rate at Primary Factor of Arcana -1 because a spell absolutely requires a minimum of factors at 1 which comes automatically with a successful casting.<br /> <br /> 2) Secondary factors in regular spells and attainments are always less than the Primary Factor because they receive the bump up in steps to Arcana -1 automatically, secondary factors are always bought up from 1 to X by accruing dice penalties. Attainments have an automatic formula for determining how many secondary factors can be &quot;bought&quot; up by saying that it's half the Arcana rating. So at Mastery half of 5 is 2.5, depending on the ST that can mean either 2 or 3 for automatic secondary factors.<br /> <br /> Looking at the PDF now though I think you're right, secondary factors calculation that I'm referring to is an artifact from my memory of the advance PDF and it was simplified for the final download. So secondary factors vary depending on the level of the prerequisite arcana for using it and are fixed instead of growing along with arcana rating like it used to. Downside, low rating attainments are screwed on secondary factors, upside high rating attainments get a significant boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that an edit then? For clarification, the book says &quot;<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.&quot;<br /> And I have no idea what that means. I can't help but feel like the example in the book is wrong anyway, because it says that a Master Force mage uses &quot;their attainment&quot; but it doesn't say what level that attainment <i>is.</i> I tried to use the Eleventh Question to figure out what the rules are saying but I feel like they contradict in parts...<br /> Your formula actually makes sense with the rules that halving and rounding up would produce those effects, but it is such a confusing example when paired with the &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; which could be either the minimum dots needed to <i>have</i> the attainment, or something else entirely in the case of conjunctional arcana attainments.<br /> Which is something else entirely cuz I didn't think that was even a <i>thing.</i><br /> The other possibility I was confused about is if that meant that the attainment gets weaker if you are using your optional arcanum, but after awhile I realized that the optional arcanum effects are practically like their own spells that modify the original attainment, not conjunctional effects at all. They can have totally different reach effects! So yeah, I'm completely confused.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077669#post1077669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the Potency bump would be 6, but the total Potency would be 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're both saying different things... If I have 6 forces, my spells/attainments should be 6 potency OR indefinite duration, right? But galivet said that the minimum arcana needed for indefinite without spell penalties is 7.<br /> Doesn't it match out like this?<br /> 1 arcana = 1 potency or 1 turn/1 hour<br /> 2 arcana = 2 potency or 2 turns/1 day<br /> 3 arcana = 3 potency or 3 turns/1 week<br /> 4 arcana = 4 potency or 4 turns/1 month<br /> 5 arcana = 5 potency or 5 turns/1 year<br /> 6 arcana = 6 potency or 6 turns/1 year+, or, indefinite with a reach and mana.<br /> <br /> Is this correct? And if so, is this decreased by 1 stage if you're using an attainment instead of an improvised spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:26:28-07:00","id":1077684,"title":"","content":"From Mage, page 198:<br /> Automatic Activation<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In most cases, a Legacy Attainment can be activated with an instant action and does not require dice rolls. Like a spell, the Attainment automatically acquires primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum minus one.<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.<br /> For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.<br /> If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two<br /> ratings.<br /> Unless specified otherwise, activating an Attainment is an instant action. Attainments cannot be enhanced by longer \u201ccasting times.\u201d </div> </div> </div>So, Duration is increased based on the user Arcana Rating, and not on the Attainment Arcana Rating. The Attainment Arcana Rating is only for Reach.<br /> <br /> Fixed Reach<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments do not use Reach in the usual way. Instead, Attainments receive only the Paradox-free Reach for meeting and exceeding Arcanum requirements, and may not Reach further. They also use the Arcanum rating of their dot, not that of the user. For example, a two-dot spell that becomes a three-dot Attainment should be designed as if it automatically has +2 Reach, even if the user actually has four dots. This lack of dynamism is one of an Attainment\u2019s disadvantages. To utilize a comparable power more flexibly, the mage should cast a spell instead. Most Attainments use one Reach for instant \u201ccasting\u201d; those that don\u2019t (being based on ritual spells) take one scene of preparation to use. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:28:27-07:00","id":1077687,"title":"","content":"Ok, so you know how when you create a character they automatically have a dot in every Attribute? Spells are like that. The Primary Factor bump of a spell or attainment are equal to Arcana -1 instead of just Arcana in order to prevent the primary factor from automatically exceeding the arcana rating of the make using the spell or attainment. Instead it equals it. So a Mage with Arcana 3 casting a Potency primary spell gets an automatic Potency of Arcana -1 and also receives another 1 point of Potency when success is achieved on the spell for a total Potency of 3.<br /> <br /> The difference between the way attainments work for secondary factors in the attainment building section and the examples provided by the 11Q legacy write up is probably an editing error that was missed in the final pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:39:55-07:00","id":1077691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077687#post1077687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so you know how when you create a character they automatically have a dot in every Attribute? Spells are like that. The Primary Factor bump of a spell or attainment are equal to Arcana -1 instead of just Arcana in order to prevent the primary factor from automatically exceeding the arcana rating of the make using the spell or attainment. Instead it equals it. So a Mage with Arcana 3 casting a Potency primary spell gets an automatic Potency of Arcana -1 and also receives another 1 point of Potency when success is achieved on the spell for a total Potency of 3.<br /> <br /> The difference between the way attainments work for secondary factors in the attainment building section and the examples provided by the 11Q legacy write up is probably an editing error that was missed in the final pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. It sounds like I understand that then, but that means that the minimum arcana for indefinite duration (barring reach problems) is 6 arcana, not 7. Although that's not going to help much--it means that any indefinite duration attainment doesn't make sense without archmastery, even if it does need 6 instead of 7.<br /> <br /> I guess that means that our problem here is if the secondary spellfactor for an attainment is supposed to be half of the mage's arcanum dots, or if it is supposed to be fixed to the dot of the attainment.<br /> Or, if it is supposed to mirror the primary factor <i>unless</i> the attainment is conjunctional, like our Forces-Spirit spell example.<br /> <br /> To make it more simple, the question I'm asking is, what the heck is the &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot;. &quot;Highest prerequisite arcanum&quot; and &quot;lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot;, by the words themselves, sound like they're the <i>exact same thing </i>if the attainment only uses 1 arcanum only, but even in the book example the Force mage is treating highest and lowest prerequisite arcanum as totally different values--and it gets even more severe when the spirit-conjunctional arcanum is thrown in.<br /> <br /> It makes sense when we use Mrmdubois's original formula that they said was in the advance pdf... because then your primary factor is arcanum and your secondary is 1/2 arcanum (I'm ignoring the minus 1 thing cuz we've talked that to death, basically, you start at the bottom of the spellfactor chart and count upwards by arcanum, starting from 0. I think we've established that is the case.)<br /> Ex. Force 5 gets 5 potency and 2.5 duration. That matches the example in the book. Force 5 Spirit 3 then gives us potency 5 and duration 1.5. That matches the example in the book too, if we round up.<br /> <br /> The description of <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>&quot;When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum,&quot; </i>doesn't match this. Am I imagining this? Please someone tell me this sounds contradictory. Because it sounds like what it is trying to say is that our Force Master mage should be getting 5 potency and 5 turns on their spell! And then 5 potency and 3 turns if their attainment is a force+spirit spell...</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:46:42-07:00","id":1077695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077691#post1077691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>&quot;When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum,&quot; </i>doesn't match this. Am I imagining this? Please someone tell me this sounds contradictory. Because it sounds like what it is trying to say is that our Force Master mage should be getting 5 potency and 5 turns on their spell! And then 5 potency and 3 turns if their attainment is a force+spirit spell...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's put things in a simple way.<br /> You cast a Attainment Forces 5 spell.<br /> <br /> It has Primary Duration. So it will last for 10 turns or 1 year.<br /> You also has 5 automatic sucess if you need those for something.<br /> <br /> The thing is, if you need to increase another spell factor, let's say, Potency, you can increase +2 Potency.<br /> Why? Cause you need to get a penalty of -4 dices to do it, and you have a pool of 5 dices.<br /> <br /> So, your otherwise Duration 5, Potency 1 spell, can have Duration 5, Potency 3(1 + 2).<br /> <br /> And now let's get a little more complicated.<br /> If the Attainment spell, for some reason, also needs Spirit, and you have Spirit 3.<br /> Now you have, for the Secondary Factors, only a pool of 3 dices to subtract.<br /> So you can only increase a secondary factor by 1 (getting a penalty of -2 dices).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-13-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:01:14-07:00","id":1077702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077695#post1077695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's put things in a simple way.<br /> You cast a Attainment Forces 5 spell.<br /> <br /> It has Primary Duration. So it will last for 10 turns or 1 year.<br /> You also has 5 automatic sucess if you need those for something.<br /> <br /> The thing is, if you need to increase another spell factor, let's say, Potency, you can increase +2 Potency.<br /> Why? Cause you need to get a penalty of -4 dices to do it, and you have a pool of 5 dices.<br /> <br /> So, your otherwise Duration 5, Potency 1 spell, can have Duration 5, Potency 3(1 + 2).<br /> <br /> And now let's get a little more complicated.<br /> If the Attainment spell, for some reason, also needs Spirit, and you have Spirit 3.<br /> Now you have, for the Secondary Factors, only a pool of 3 dices to subtract.<br /> So you can only increase a secondary factor by 1 (getting a penalty of -2 dices).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that sounds more interesting. But only because I think I see the problem. The book says, specifically,<span style=\"font-family:arial\"> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast<span style=\"color:#000000\"> as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.&quot;<br /> I took this to mean entire spellfactor <i>ranks</i>, just like how the primary factor gets <i>ranks.</i><br /> <br /> What you're saying is, </span></span>&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast<span style=\"color:#000000\"> as a spell) up to <b>dice</b> <b>equal to</b> the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> So lowest prerequisite arcanum isn't ranks but dice.<br /> Primary spellfactor uses ranks.<br /> Secondary uses dice, or, basically, half-ranks.<br /> <br /> 5 Forces attainment has primary 5 ranks, and secondary 5 dice (which are used to gain ranks at -2 each).<br /> <br /> Is this correct?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:06:43-07:00","id":1077704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077702#post1077702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 Forces attainment has primary 5 ranks, and secondary 5 dice (which are used to gain ranks at -2 each).<br /> Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the book:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> So, yes. It's pretty much what you said.<br /> To get an additional spell factor you need a -2 penalty dice.<br /> So, having the Lowest Arcana involved at level 2 or 4 will give you +1 or +2 secondary spell factors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:11:32-07:00","id":1077707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077704#post1077704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the book:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> So, yes. It's pretty much what you said.<br /> To get an additional spell factor you need a -2 penalty dice.<br /> So, having the Lowest Arcana involved at level 2 or 4 will give you +1 or +2 secondary spell factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me that's not easy to figure out. Cuz that is <i>really</i> not easy to figure out. None of my Mage-player friends were able to figure this out either. When juxtaposed with the preceding paragraph it sounds like it is talking about entire ranks, not using the arcanum as a numeral and then taking ranks out of it at -2's.<br /> <br /> I guess I got this mostly figured out then. I guess the only thing that confuses me now is if attainments using conjunctional arcana is optional or if including one makes the attainment <i>fixed</i> on that and you can no longer take it back. Like, if you have a shape-changing 5th attainment and you use matter 4 in it so that your clothes change with you, is that now an attainment that forever requires matter 4 or if you can just build up to it.<br /> <br /> But I can see why the OP was saying that indefinite duration is impractical for attainments. Unless the ST allows an attainment to use Lasting as an option, it sounds really, really bad.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your patient help :c<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:21:16-07:00","id":1077714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077707#post1077707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please tell me that's not easy to figure out. Cuz that is <i>really</i> not easy to figure out. None of my Mage-player friends were able to figure this out either. When juxtaposed with the preceding paragraph it sounds like it is talking about entire ranks, not using the arcanum as a numeral and then taking ranks out of it at -2's.<br /> <br /> I guess I got this mostly figured out then. I guess the only thing that confuses me now is if attainments using conjunctional arcana is optional or if including one makes the attainment <i>fixed</i> on that and you can no longer take it back. Like, if you have a shape-changing 5th attainment and you use matter 4 in it so that your clothes change with you, is that now an attainment that forever requires matter 4 or if you can just build up to it.<br /> <br /> But I can see why the OP was saying that indefinite duration is impractical for attainments. Unless the ST allows an attainment to use Lasting as an option, it sounds really, really bad.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your patient help :c</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me a while to figure it out. Every time I try to understand a complicate rule I boil it to just mathematic formulas.<br /> <br /> Analyzing the sentence:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> <br /> You have a additional spell factor that would incur a penalty up to the attainments lowest prerequisite Arcanum:<br /> Let's say that it is Mind 4<br /> So, the maximum penalty I can have is -4.<br /> -4 is penalty enough for getting +2 spell factors.<br /> That's how I figured it out.<br /> <br /> Now to your second question:<br /> <i>Like, if you have a shape-changing 5th attainment and you use matter 4 in it so that your clothes change with you, is that now an attainment that forever requires matter 4 or if you can just build up to it.</i><br /> Powers like this usually specify that &quot;if&quot; you have this, you &quot;can&quot; use it that way. So, IMHO, I think that you can chose the effect when you use the power.<br /> People usually tend to look at Attainment as highly static powers, but the only static part of the Attainments, by the book, are the Reach effects.<br /> So, for me, unless the power specify that you can only use it that way, you can integrate the other arcana effects into it, if you have those and they don't cost Reach and don't go against the philosophy of your Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:28:02-07:00","id":1077717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077714#post1077714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It took me a while to figure it out. Every time I try to understand a complicate rule I boil it to just mathematic formulas.<br /> <br /> Analyzing the sentence:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> <br /> You have a additional spell factor that would incur a penalty up to the attainments lowest prerequisite Arcanum:<br /> Let's say that it is Mind 4<br /> So, the maximum penalty I can have is -4.<br /> -4 is penalty enough for getting +2 spell factors.<br /> That's how I figured it out.<br /> <br /> Now to your second question:<br /> <i>Like, if you have a shape-changing 5th attainment and you use matter 4 in it so that your clothes change with you, is that now an attainment that forever requires matter 4 or if you can just build up to it.</i><br /> Powers like this usually specify that &quot;if&quot; you have this, you &quot;can&quot; use it that way. So, IMHO, I think that you can chose the effect when you use the power.<br /> People usually tend to look at Attainment as highly static powers, but the only static part of the Attainments, by the book, are the Reach effects.<br /> So, for me, unless the power specify that you can only use it that way, you can integrate the other arcana effects into it, if you have those and they don't cost Reach and don't go against the philosophy of your Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do you think that Attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle would work on Legacy Attainments, and <i>if so</i> do they then become <i>mandatory.</i> Like if a Time legacy that has mastigos as its path makes all the attainments utilize Everywhere and Time in a Bottle to maximize their power and utility, the legacy suddenly becomes unusuable until the mage is a 2nd degree adept? ((If so, I'm guessing this means the legacy can be learned easily, but the attainments become impossible until the mage is very experienced, but woah would those be some attainments!))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:32:27-07:00","id":1077718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077717#post1077717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do you think that Attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle would work on Legacy Attainments, and <i>if so</i> do they then become <i>mandatory.</i> Like if a Time legacy that has mastigos as its path makes all the attainments utilize Everywhere and Time in a Bottle to maximize their power and utility, the legacy suddenly becomes unusuable until the mage is a 2nd degree adept? ((If so, I'm guessing this means the legacy can be learned easily, but the attainments become impossible until the mage is very experienced, but woah would those be some attainments!))</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Prophecy in the 11Q utilizes Sympathy (And not the Temporal kind) but doesn't require Space then I assume that a legacy attainment can use some Arcana Attainments at the appropriate level without any other prerequisite. Not sure though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:35:25-07:00","id":1077723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077717#post1077717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do you think that Attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle would work on Legacy Attainments, and <i>if so</i> do they then become <i>mandatory.</i> Like if a Time legacy that has mastigos as its path makes all the attainments utilize Everywhere and Time in a Bottle to maximize their power and utility, the legacy suddenly becomes unusuable until the mage is a 2nd degree adept? ((If so, I'm guessing this means the legacy can be learned easily, but the attainments become impossible until the mage is very experienced, but woah would those be some attainments!))</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since they modify the Reach options, I think that no. On my last anwser I was referring to Optional effects based on your other Arcanas.<br /> I don't know if you can integrate the use of an Arcana Attainment on a Legacy Attainment. You probably can, but maybe as a fixed pre-requisite, since it alters how some Reach works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:35:53-07:00","id":1077724,"title":"","content":"Spell Factors for Attainments, 101:<br /> Primary Factor = Arcana Rating of highest Arcana used in Attainment<br /> Secondary Factors = Half of Arcana Rating of lowest Arcana used in Attainment (round up/down, according to ST preference).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:37:10-07:00","id":1077725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077718#post1077718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering Prophecy in the 11Q utilizes Sympathy (And not the Temporal kind) but doesn't require Space then I assume that a legacy attainment can use some Arcana Attainments at the appropriate level without any other prerequisite. Not sure though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah cuz the sympathy thing is sort of <i>needed, </i>it isn't there for giggles. It is a totally different beast. It might be a thing where it has to fit the spirit of the attainment. Kinda like how around the forum there is discussion on if the automatic successes apply to clash of wills or can create an exceptional success, but the book also says the successes are only used when required, which kinda implies that they're not there just for power, they're there to settle disputes... ...<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:56:34-07:00","id":1077739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077725#post1077725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah cuz the sympathy thing is sort of <i>needed, </i>it isn't there for giggles. It is a totally different beast. It might be a thing where it has to fit the spirit of the attainment. Kinda like how around the forum there is discussion on if the automatic successes apply to clash of wills or can create an exceptional success, but the book also says the successes are only used when required, which kinda implies that they're not there just for power, they're there to settle disputes... ...<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's not needed for that attainment in the 11Q, it could have stayed the same as the spell and only been useful on subjects actually present (in default at least), but instead it said you could cast Sympathetically via a Representational Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:28:03-07:00","id":1077769,"title":"","content":"The main vehicle for flavoring legacy attainments is taking advantage of the &quot;atypical&quot; allowance to make the attainment slightly more powerful but substantially more niche than its corresponding spell.<br /> <br /> The rank 4 11Q attainment is clearly &quot;Like Prophecy, but it only works for this one niche kind of thing, but also somehow you get to use Sympathetic magic without including Space.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since all 2E legacies are homebrew except for 11Q, ST approval is important for the particulars of legacy attainments. I'm just trying to discuss guidelines for mechanics that should not be at all controversial based on RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:20:37-07:00","id":1077844,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I have no idea how to make atypical attainments properly atypical...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:49:37-07:00","id":1077859,"title":"","content":"It's a four step process:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Think to yourself, &quot;This would be a cool attainment if only it could also manage X, but the rules don't permit that.&quot;</li> <li>Go ahead and make the attainment able to do X so it can be worth using</li> <li>Realize that your ST will see the attainment as &quot;unbalanced&quot;</li> <li>Throw in a few thematically-appropriate circumstantial restrictions so that the attainment really only useful in situations that the ST builds into the story to let it shine</li> </ol>Example<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This attainment to predict the future crimes of a suspect would be awesome... except that if the suspect is around for to use this on him,, then that probably means I already caught the guy. Pointless. I need to be able to use it against a subject who's still a fugitive. Arggh, but Space isn't part of this legacy. Even if Space was part of the legacy, the skimpy number of Potency I get to work with won't let me overcome the Withstand for the sympathetic range casting. The rules just aren't supporting me here.</li> <li>Fuck it, I'm saying it works on fugitives too. I have no idea what else I could do for a rank 4 attainment for this legacy; this has got to be it, rules-be-damned.</li> <li>Well... Gary probably isn't going to let this fly as-is. I gotta throw him some bones somehow.</li> <li>Uh, so it only works if I have the information on the guy to build a profile. And it takes a long time to use; I'll blow the reach on sensory range for no good reason. And it takes a sympathy yantra. And I'll blow the Optional Matter effect on something that doesn't really expand the utility of the attainment. Yeah, so now I'll only get to use this if Gary tees it up for me. We'll both be happy.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:10:37-07:00","id":1077872,"title":"","content":"But what if I'm the ST :V?<br /> <br /> And both from player and ST perspective alike, I don't like the idea that something should be &quot;only useful&quot; in situations &quot;built in the story&quot;, mostly because we prefer players to take initiative and actively create opportunities for using their stuff, not to wait for a carefully built opportunity, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:30:17-07:00","id":1077882,"title":"","content":"There are a ton of player capabilities in Mage that are only useful if the ST builds opportunities into the story for them to shine. Spells related to curing/resisting poisons or diseases, spells dealing with Extreme Envionments, the entire Spirit arcanum, etc... Atypical legacy attainments aren't unique in that regard..<br /> <br /> My opinion is that only the ST gets to decide when the players can break the rules of the game. So if a player has a legacy attainment that breaks the rules of the game, then the ST decides when the player gets to use it. If you're the ST, you can approve anything you like.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to be in the position of judging such attainments, the guidelines in the OP result in attainments that are useful and that follow the rules strictly. Does it result in cookie-cutter legacy attainments? Sure... but when you consider the thematic variations enabled by following the template for each of the ten Arcana, that's still a hell of a lot more variety than is available to e.g. a vampire picking between Cruac and Lancea Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:50:40-07:00","id":1077939,"title":"","content":"4. Sensory is there because spells that use Sympathy are cast at Sensory Range, and the Matter 4 part forces the environment to cough up the requisite materials and data to use the Time part which effectively removes the need for ST caveat.<br /> <br /> I think the design decision was that most attainments are designed to be Instant, and Prophecy is really useful as an Instant spell unless you have Sympathy because then you could ritual it at leisure so it balances out since it requires a ritual to activate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:55:57-07:00","id":1077944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077882#post1077882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a ton of player capabilities in Mage that are only useful if the ST builds opportunities into the story for them to shine. Spells related to curing/resisting poisons or diseases, spells dealing with Extreme Envionments, the entire Spirit arcanum, etc... Atypical legacy attainments aren't unique in that regard..<br /> <br /> My opinion is that only the ST gets to decide when the players can break the rules of the game. So if a player has a legacy attainment that breaks the rules of the game, then the ST decides when the player gets to use it. If you're the ST, you can approve anything you like.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you don't want to be in the position of judging such attainments, the guidelines in the OP result in attainments that are useful and that follow the rules strictly. Does it result in cookie-cutter legacy attainments? Sure... but when you consider the thematic variations enabled by following the template for each of the ten Arcana, that's still a hell of a lot more variety than is available to e.g. a vampire picking between Cruac and Lancea Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can dig it. My own ST decided to only use the rules as a rough guideline because it made remaking The Pure Sovereigns really difficult to reproduce, especially since the cookie-cutter rules do not explain how to do &quot;always on&quot; attainments unless you have it as Lasting or something. In exchange, the attainments of the Pure Sovereign only work on the Blue Blood--you cannot perform the attainment on someone else with a touch-and-ritual or something. So, makes sense. Although I do not think the 11th Question attainments do that, I think the intention was that they were a de-facto cookie cutter legacy. I could be wrong though... ...<br /> <br /> Thanks for posting this topic though, I think your heuristics are really on point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077939#post1077939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Sensory is there because spells that use Sympathy are cast at Sensory Range, and the Matter 4 part forces the environment to cough up the requisite materials and data to use the Time part which effectively removes the need for ST caveat.<br /> <br /> I think the design decision was that most attainments are designed to be Instant, and Prophecy is really useful as an Instant spell unless you have Sympathy because then you could ritual it at leisure so it balances out since it requires a ritual to activate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just realized something weird about what you said. If it was using the sympathy utility attainment, shouldn't The Timely Answer cost 1 mana? :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:01:19-07:00","id":1077950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077944#post1077944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can dig it. My own ST decided to only use the rules as a rough guideline because it made remaking The Pure Sovereigns really difficult to reproduce, especially since the cookie-cutter rules do not explain how to do &amp;quot;always on&amp;quot; attainments unless you have it as Lasting or something. In exchange, the attainments of the Pure Sovereign only work on the Blue Blood--you cannot perform the attainment on someone else with a touch-and-ritual or something. So, makes sense. Although I do not think the 11th Question attainments do that, I think the intention was that they were a de-facto cookie cutter legacy. I could be wrong though... ...<br /> <br /> Thanks for posting this topic though, I think your heuristics are really on point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just realized something weird about what you said. If it was using the sympathy utility attainment, shouldn't The Timely Answer cost 1 mana? :O</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Always on&quot; attainments aren't hard, give it Advanced Duration, renew its Duration before it expires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:30:51-07:00","id":1077975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077950#post1077950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Always on&quot; attainments aren't hard, give it Advanced Duration, renew its Duration before it expires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so too, my ST hated the idea of that though. Anywho, I am starting to think that I am wrong about the 11th Question attainments all being pure examples of the &quot;make your own attainment&quot; rules, because The Penultimate Answer's Optional Matter effect apparently has instant <i>and</i> sensory use. Unless it is saying that it has sensory use and it isn't instant use because you already did the &quot;ritual&quot; in the past? I don't get it. But the time arcanum is weird anyway...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:54:11-07:00","id":1077988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077975#post1077975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so too, my ST hated the idea of that though. Anywho, I am starting to think that I am wrong about the 11th Question attainments all being pure examples of the &amp;quot;make your own attainment&amp;quot; rules, because The Penultimate Answer's Optional Matter effect apparently has instant <i>and</i> sensory use. Unless it is saying that it has sensory use and it isn't instant use because you already did the &amp;quot;ritual&amp;quot; in the past? I don't get it. But the time arcanum is weird anyway...</div> </div> </div> </div>That last attainment is essentially a Combined Spell type effect, the &quot;Instant&quot; Matter part is only possible because of the ritual activation of the Time part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:04:02-07:00","id":1077994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077988#post1077988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last attainment is essentially a Combined Spell type effect, the &quot;Instant&quot; Matter part is only possible because of the ritual activation of the Time part.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was right? But that's also so weird! My visceral reaction is to just shout &quot;that's even allowed?!&quot; but if it wasn't the 11th Question wouldn't be usable. I guess wiggling around on the specifics is pretty much essential after-awhile. Until Dave said that the Tremere were intended to be an altered version of the Mage template, I had originally tried to make my own tremere legacy so I could have an antagonist (I was going to name him Hungry Jack :3 ) but I couldn't figure out how I was supposed to make severing souls and soul jars practical and usable on a 3 attainment budget.<br /> <br /> And don't even get me started on Dreamspeakers, that legacy is making me cry!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:06:32-07:00","id":1077998,"title":"","content":"What's hard about the Dreamspeakers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:46:09-07:00","id":1078051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077939#post1077939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Sensory is there because spells that use Sympathy are cast at Sensory Range, and the Matter 4 part forces the environment to cough up the requisite materials and data to use the Time part which effectively removes the need for ST caveat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure... although spells cast using sympathy also use the sympathetic range withstand. For an object assembled using magic out of &quot;impressions from the past or emanations from the future&quot;, I'm guessing that would be a Weak sympathy yantra. A mage with Time 4 who just learned this attainment has 100% of her successes consumed by the sympathy withstand and the power is useless. Consequently I guess we're meant to neglect sympathy withstand for this attainment. If you're willing to do that, are you really concerned about spending that one reach properly? It's a bit like polishing the headlamps on a totaled car.<br /> <br /> Taking a step back, would you allow a Time 4 + Matter 4 conjunctional spell to create a functioning sympathy yantra out of whatever detritus is the vicinity of a mage who is &quot;building a profile of known data about a subject... entirely in her mind&quot;? I wouldn't. Even if I would, the yantra is created <i>at the conclusion</i> of casting that conjunctional spell, so it can't be used to facilitate the sympathetic casting of that very spell, right?<br /> <br /> Basically rule-wise that attainment is a big bag of nonsense. And sometimes that's what it takes to make a sympathy attainment interesting or useful, and why the rules allow such &quot;atypical&quot; attainments -- with ST approval. This is apparently kosher under the rubric of &quot;These adjustments shouldn\u2019t make Attainments significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-13-2017, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:28:41-07:00","id":1078073,"title":"","content":"I don't personally find it a big bag of nonsense, with Time 4 you can probably exceed their Withstand at Time 4 anyway even with a Sympathetic Withstand and there isn't any indication that the effect of the 4th attainment is combined. I think it would actually require you to use the Matter attainment and -then- the Time attainment separately. Matter by itself could certainly provide the Yantra, considering a Representational Yantra isn't that hard to render.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T20:32:05-07:00","id":1078150,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, maybe it's not so bad as I make it out.<br /> <br /> A Time 4 mage is working with 3 potency. After tanking into account sympathetic withstand, she needs to have one Potency remaining to ask one question. Based on the purpose of the attainment, I think it's usually a safe assumption that she doesn't know the subject's sympathetic name; that increases the withstand level by one. So that means that the sympathetic yantra &quot;found&quot; via the optional Matter facet of the attainment needs to be a Strong yantra, equivalent to finding the subject's dedicated magical tool. Feels like a stretch.<br /> <br /> If the mage uses the Matter attainment first, and it's exclusively Matter, then I don't know where the &quot;impressions from the past or emanations from the future&quot; that are somehow specific to the subject of the Time attainment come from. It seems like you would need those to form a sympathetic yantra specific to that subject. I suppose the mage would need to get those impressions and emanations by incorporating the Time arcanum. But you can't use the Time arcanum for such a purpose without the subject present because you don't yet have the sympathetic yantra. It's a catch-22. However we justify the creation of the sympathetic yantra to begin with, that same justification ought to be good enough for just casting the Time attainment (Prophecy) without subject present <b>and </b>without the sympathetic yantra.<br /> <br /> &quot;Big bag of nonsense&quot; is a bit harsh, but I don't think this is something you could accomplish with creative thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-13-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T02:57:59-07:00","id":1078244,"title":"","content":"Prophecy isn't Withstood except by Sympathetic Distance, with a name the 4th attainment could create a weak link and the Mage could get and still get one question, without the name it would have to be a medium connection, but the attainment doesn't specify what level of connection it provides it simply assumes that the level is strong enough for the Time attainment to work. <br /> <br /> To my reading the bit about the impressions of the past and emanations from the future is just there as fluff, and it holds the door open for the ST, not the player to choose the specific Yantra that's generated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:13:24-07:00","id":1078250,"title":"","content":"It is kind of weird in general isn't it? The benefit of attainments is that they are paradox free, but using these on sleepers also kinda implies scenarios where you'd wanna just down-and-dirty the magic anyway so maybe that's why you're supposed to fudge it? Because the 11th Question would mostly be using it to be superlative cops? I dunno.<br /> <br /> It's just weird cuz The Timely Answer specifically says &quot;representational yantra&quot;... but why? It isn't like that +1 die is useful, you can't use it. Maybe they meant it would help with the withstand or that the purpose of this thing is to negate withstand anyway? Or it already assumes the potency is so high that nothing short of magic is going to prevent the spell from working?<br /> <br /> It's too bad that legacies couldn't have gotten just <i>one</i> more page dedicated to it. Could you imagine the breathing room that they could have had with it. But I'd imagine that would have made significant impacts on the cost to print the books. Ah well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:18:18-07:00","id":1078251,"title":"","content":"I assume it's specifically Representation Yantra because it allows the broadest range of options for materials to be generated and can be the most clue-like.<br /> <br /> The +1 certainly can be used though if the 11Q keeps the object and uses it against his target as a part of a spell later on in the big, in person showdown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T05:24:18-07:00","id":1078283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1078244#post1078244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prophecy isn't Withstood except by Sympathetic Distance, with a name the 4th attainment could create a weak link and the Mage could get and still get one question, without the name it would have to be a medium connection, but the attainment doesn't specify what level of connection it provides it simply assumes that the level is strong enough for the Time attainment to work.<br /> <br /> To my reading the bit about the impressions of the past and emanations from the future is just there as fluff, and it holds the door open for the ST, not the player to choose the specific Yantra that's generated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it seems like it would be important to know that detail about the strength of the connection because it determines how many questions you get to ask per activation of the attainment. It takes a scene to activate so being able to ask one question per scene spent versus two questions per scene spent is a big deal. This is why I think that the intent of the attainment is to throw the sympathetic withstand rule out of the window. Nevertheless, with a Weak link the sympathetic range withstand is 3 and then +1 for not knowing the sympathetic name, so I'm not sure how your math works out here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: vvvvvv weak, I retract vvvvv<br /> <br /> Also it seems like you're saying that if I literally had Matter 4 sitting in my chair here, I could conjure a representational yantra out of stuff in my office for any other person in the world, despite having no preexisting sympathetic link with the person. If you think Matter 4 can do that, I don't know where to go. Besides which, the description of the Matter attainment does say &quot;Time and Matter conspire...&quot; so I really believe it's a conjunctional effect.<br /> <br /> One last rules hole: The reach for the Matter attainment is spent on instant casting, or maybe on sensory range, it's not clear. It's sure not spent on Advanced Duration though. Assuming that the Matter attainment is Duration primary and the caster has Matter 4, the sympathy yantra lasts for three turns. Meanwhile the Time attainment takes a whole scene to activate. The sympathy yantra decays less than ten seconds into the scene-long activation of the Time attainment. I think that would interrupt the activation. I guess you can claim that the sympathy yantra creation is Lasting; in that case the Matter component is <i>really badass</i> because you can instantly create permanent sympathy yantras for anyone and then use them to cast anything you want on that subject. Or you could give it to another mage to use for some other spell. You could form a sympathy yantra for every Seer of the Throne for whom you can &quot;build a profile of known data&quot; about, then hand them over to the Arrow for use in war.I feel like it gets absurd.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ^^^^^^ weak, I retract ^^^^^<br /> <br /> EDIT: That last paragraph (&quot;One last rules hole&quot;) really isn't good. Of course the creation of the representational yantra is lasting, and it's not a big deal at all. I could easily prevent abuse as the ST by setting the standard of earlier investigative work needed to activate the attainment (building the profile, the profile has to be X complete before the attainment works). The context clearly implies that the mage has been engaged in a significant investigation of the subject. That should certainly be sufficient to create a representational yantra of the subject using Matter 4.<br /> <br /> I'm still murky on the application of the sympathetic casting rules for this attainment, though, and I still believe that the intent of the attainment is not to apply those rules. But I also might just not understand the rules for sympathetic casting properly. vOv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:40:56-07:00","id":1078306,"title":"","content":"Matter 4 could create a Representation Yantra for anyone, yeah, Matter can do &quot;old&quot; photographs or whatever without too much trouble I imagine. It would work as the Sympathy Yantra, but wouldn't have any Sympathy to borrow in order to use it as a Sympathetic connection for the casting. I imagine that over the course of the investigation an 11Q will have developed that on their own between themselves and their target the old fashioned way, so they only need the material Sympathetic Yantra to use the Sympathy attainment anyway, not for its connection to the target.<br /> <br /> Anyway, its true it would have been nice if they had written it all up in a clearer way. It may have been intended for the attainment to simply meet the requirements for using Sympathy but then ignore the actual Sympathy rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:49:06-07:00","id":1078310,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the back-and-forth; it was very useful for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:28:34-07:00","id":1078370,"title":"","content":"My pleasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:51:19-07:00","id":1078549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1078306#post1078306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matter 4 could create a Representation Yantra for anyone, yeah, Matter can do &quot;old&quot; photographs or whatever without too much trouble I imagine. It would work as the Sympathy Yantra, but wouldn't have any Sympathy to borrow in order to use it as a Sympathetic connection for the casting. I imagine that over the course of the investigation an 11Q will have developed that on their own between themselves and their target the old fashioned way, so they only need the material Sympathetic Yantra to use the Sympathy attainment anyway, not for its connection to the target.<br /> <br /> Anyway, its true it would have been nice if they had written it all up in a clearer way. It may have been intended for the attainment to simply meet the requirements for using Sympathy but then ignore the actual Sympathy rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gosh, that's brilliant! That has to be it! And if we assume the yantra disappears after an hour or something, in the form of misplacement or anything else short of vanishing before someone's eyes, we have a little less potential shenanigans abuse (although them being from the Guardians I guess they wouldn't do that crap anyway?)<br /> So what kind of sympathetic connection do you think they could get through this? Weak only or Medium? It sounds like Medium is the bare minimum to get 1 question, unless that satchel person was right on the Awakened Questions topic and that the additional spellfactors *could* apply to potency, which would get us 2 questions on weak symapthy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:48:13-07:00","id":1078598,"title":"","content":"Well, if I'm right that it actually uses the strength of Sympathy that the 11Q has to his quarry (built up via investigation) rather than borrowing any from the Yantra then the level of Sympathetic strength will vary depending on how invested in the chase the 11Q has become. So, if for instance this is his first move in the investigation then it will probably be Weak, but the more time and effort put into it the stronger the Sympathy will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T12:47:01-07:00","id":1079007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1077525-guidelines-for-especially-useful-legacy-attainments?p=1077769#post1077769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all 2E legacies are homebrew except for 11Q, ST approval is important for the particulars of legacy attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also check out the Nagaraja Legacy from To The Strongest chapter of Dark Eras.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}